codex
I found the cause: this audit container’s process IDs are namespaced, but `/proc` is mounted from a different PID namespace. Lean 4.22 resolves its executable via `/proc/<getpid()>/exe`, which is absent here, while `/proc/self/exe` works; that breaks both Lean and Lake installation detection. I’m applying a narrow runtime shim that redirects only that executable-path read to `/proc/self/exe`, recording its source and use, then rerunning the unmodified trusted preflight.
apply patch
